<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Mazrui Sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1741 CE – 1837 CE (approx.) · capital Mombasa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The rule of the Omani Mazrui family over Mombasa, which broke away from Oman and resisted its sultans for nearly a century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-jesus">Fort Jesus</a> from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/portuguese-mombasa">Portuguese Mombasa</a> in 1698, it appointed governors from the Mazrui clan. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaruba-dynasty">Ya'rubid dynasty</a> of Oman fell in 1741, the governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-uthman-al-mazrui">Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Mazrui</a> refused to recognise the new Busaidi rulers and made <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mombasa">Mombasa</a> independent.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Mazrui ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-jesus">Fort Jesus</a> as governors-turned-sovereigns, allied with the twelve <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> clans of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mombasa">Mombasa</a> and with mainland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mijikenda">Mijikenda</a> communities. At their height they controlled the coast from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pemba-island">Pemba</a> to Pate. Facing the Busaidi, they sought British protection, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-fitzwilliam-owen">Captain William Owen</a> declared a short-lived <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in 1824 that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> disowned in 1826.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/said-bin-sultan">Sayyid Said of Oman</a> conquered <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mombasa">Mombasa</a> in 1837 and deported leading Mazrui. Branches of the family moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gazi-kenya">Gazi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takaungu">Takaungu</a> on the Kenyan coast, and some rebelled against British rule in 1895 to 1896.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1741 CE – 1837 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">sultanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Horn and East Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:94.35%;width:1.91%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1741 CE – 1837 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mombasa</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Mazrui</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Swahili, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/kenya">Kenya</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mazrui Mombasa, Mazrui dynasty of Mombasa</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1789&amp;focus=mazrui-sultanate" aria-label="Mazrui Sultanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5781 2329 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Mazrui Sultanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6101 2585L6562 1563"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6562 1563h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6101 2585h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6101 2585h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mombasa. <a href="/atlas?year=1789&amp;focus=mazrui-sultanate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
